    "focal_region": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 1 USER]\ne001\tOur eight-person policy research team is considering replacing two weekly status meetings with one written update and one optional problem-solving session.\ne002\tSome people think meetings create accountability; others say they consume the uninterrupted time needed for analysis.\ne003\tI want to test the change without turning it into another permanent process decree.\n[Turn 1 ASSISTANT]\ne004\tTreat it as a reversible work-design experiment.\ne005\tDefine what should improve, what must not degrade, whose experience matters, and when the team will decide whether to keep, adjust, or stop it.\n[Turn 7 USER]\ne034\tAgreed.\ne035\tWe will run the four weeks, publish the weekly measures to the team, trigger restoration if two gates fail at week two, and make no permanence claim before the anonymous vote and evidence review.\ne036\tNothing else is unresolved for me now.\n[Turn 7 ASSISTANT]\ne037\tThen the decision process is complete enough to proceed.\ne038\tThe trial is reversible, the evidence standard predates commitment, contrary experience has a protected channel, and both early and final decision rules are explicit.\ne039\tRecord the results and follow the rules already chosen; no additional reasoning pressure is presently warranted.",
